bl:AC_StoryCorpusContract a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json is loadable, cross-reference-clean, and disclosure-preserving"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json, When a developer or the instantiation script loads it, Then all 6 required top-level keys (MISSION, CATEGORIES, PRINCIPLES, FRAMEWORKS, RELATIONS, CITATIONS) are present and every cross-reference among them (a PRINCIPLE's cat, fw and reinforces entries; a RELATION's source and target) resolves to a real id rather than failing silently. And When a reader searches the PRINCIPLES text for the two previously-disclosed evidentiary limitations (the Amplitude figures, the GitLab conflict-of-interest note), Then both are found verbatim in the running prose, not only referenced by citation number." .

bl:Evidence_TaskAuthorCorpusJSON a backlog:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json exists, parses, and satisfies the schema and STORY-1's disclosure requirement"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checked directly, this session: (1) file exists at code-abundance-rdodi/04-interactive-page/01-corpus-contract/corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json, 46524 bytes; (2) python3 json.load succeeds; (3) all 6 required top-level keys present (MISSION, CATEGORIES, PRINCIPLES, FRAMEWORKS, RELATIONS, CITATIONS) matching 01-schema/corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json; (4) 18 PRINCIPLES (matching Stage 2's 18 leaf classes exactly), 7 CATEGORIES (matching Stage 2's 7 top-level classes), 15 CITATIONS (matching Stage 1's 15 Publications); (5) every reinforces/cat/fw/RELATIONS source-target reference resolves to a real id -- one broken reference (a non-existent 'CursorAmplitude' id) found and fixed during this check, not before it; (6) the 2 disclosed evidentiary limitations (Amplitude figures, GitLab COI) confirmed present verbatim in the PRINCIPLES text itself (ExecutionPillar, DeveloperDemandCritique, MetricValidityAndSelectionBiasCritique, CodeIsPreciousConstraint, GitLabDuoAgentPlatform), not just referenced in the citation list -- satisfying STORY-1's own rescoped requirement." .

bl:AC_StoryQuizAndGlossary a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "Every PRINCIPLE's apply field is genuinely distinct, non-templated content"@en ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json's 18 PRINCIPLES, When a reader compares any two entries' apply fields, Then they read as genuinely different practical guidance specific to that concept, not the same sentence with the label substituted. And When counted programmatically, Then the number of distinct apply strings equals the number of principles (18 of 18), and none starts with a shared templated prefix." .

bl:Evidence_StoryQuizAndGlossary a backlog:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage bl:CodeAbundanceLineage ;
    rdfs:label "corpus_contract_v1_0_0.json's 18 apply fields are genuinely distinct, checked programmatically"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-09-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Checked directly, this session: (1) all 18 PRINCIPLES' apply fields rewritten with content specific to that concept's own argument, drawn from the real Stage 3 text; (2) python3 check: 18 total, 18 distinct strings; (3) python3 check: 0 entries still start with the old templated prefix 'When evaluating a similar claim, check what this report checked'; (4) confirmed the real template tab list (Overview, Principle Explorer, Interact, Citations, About) directly from the source HTML, not assumed -- Citations tab is already fed by STORY-1's 15 real citations; Principle Explorer is already fed by the 18 real principles; Overview corresponds to MISSION, already present. Quiz dropped per explicit owner instruction; Glossary role treated as satisfied by the principles' own real short/en_short fields, the mechanism's actual equivalent, not a separate structure with nowhere to render." .

