    backlog:asRole "a reader of the interactive companion" ;
    backlog:wantsCapability "each real section the template actually provides (Overview, Principle Explorer, Citations) fed with substantive, non-templated content -- rescoped from the original 'quiz and glossary' framing after checking the real mechanism, not assumed" ;
    backlog:soThat "the reader gets real, distinct, per-concept guidance rather than templated filler -- found and fixed during this Story: STORY-1's own 'apply' field had been the same generic sentence with only the label substituted, across all 18 principles, never caught by the structural checks that closed STORY-1 (references-resolve, disclosures-present), which checked structure, not content quality. Quiz dropped per owner instruction (not necessary); Glossary role treated as satisfied by the principles' own real short/en_short definitions, which is what the mechanism actually provides -- not a separate authored glossary structure with nowhere to render. Introduction/Body/References are the real tabs the template ships (Overview/Principle Explorer/Citations), confirmed directly against the template source, not assumed from the procedure document alone." ;
    backlog:partOf bl:EpicAdoptRichDefault ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective bl:ObjRDODIDefaultGatesPassing .

